   "title": "Start here",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## MiniMax H3 AIO - start here\n\n1. **Pick a mode** in the AIO node. The grey line under it says what to load.\n2. **Load media** in the Media Loader (Picture 1, Video 1, Audio 1 ...).\n3. **Write the prompt** in the AIO node - or, for **Long** modes and **Extend Video**, write the whole video as one story in the **Seamless Planner** (it splits it into clips for you; read them in *Plan*).\n4. **Run.** Watch it in *Live Preview*; the result lands in *Video result* (or *Image result* for Image Editing).\n\nEvery H3 node has an **(i) How to use** button with the full guide for that node / mode.\n\n**Side nodes:** Speed & Quality (steps, turbo, Spectrum, upscale detail), Seamless Settings (how clips join), Models and LoRAs (set once). Unplug any of them and sensible defaults are used.\n\n**Memory:** prompts are encoded once and the 15 GB text encoder is released before the video model loads; if RAM is short the AIO frees memory first and says so in *Run info*. Start ComfyUI with run_comfyui_minimax_h3.bat (no --cache-lru)."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## MiniMax H3 AIO - start here\n\n1. **Pick a mode** in the AIO node. The grey line under it says what to load.\n2. **Load media** in the Media Loader (Picture 1, Video 1, Audio 1 ...).\n3. **Write the prompt** in the AIO node - or, for **Long** modes and **Extend Video**, write the whole video as one story in the **Seamless Planner** (it splits it into clips for you; read them in *Plan*).\n4. **Run.** Watch it in *Live Preview*; the result lands in *Video result* (or *Image result* for Image Editing).\n\nEvery H3 node has an **(i) How to use** button with the full guide for that node / mode.\n\n**Side nodes:** Speed & Quality (steps, turbo, Spectrum, upscale detail), Seamless Settings (how clips join), Models and LoRAs (set once). Unplug any of them and sensible defaults are used.\n\n**Memory:** prompts are encoded once and the 15 GB text encoder is released before the video model loads; if RAM is short the AIO frees memory first and says so in *Run info*. Start ComfyUI with run_comfyui_minimax_h3.bat (no --cache-lru)."
   },
